{title: Song of the Young People}
{key: G}
{reviewed: false}

{section: Verse 1}
[G]We shout with joy, we rise and sing! The [C]Will of God [Am]is [D7]done!
[G]A new day dawns and the [Am]dream lives; the [D]Son [D7]of [G]God has come!
[Em]Fight bravely to crush Satan; God's power will be [B]revealed.
[G]In the children of our Father, the [Am]Youth of [D]Harmony.

{section: Verse 2}
The darkness which has covered us in Him has been dispelled.
The dawn breaks into daylight; we ring the morning bell.
Thirty billion shall live in the bright white light of truth.
Let us rise and march forward with Harmony of Youth.

{section: Verse 3}
As children of the Heavenly power, we march against our foe;
The command comes and the world bows to our True Father's own!
Beaming light unto the nations, we carry high our dream. Let us win
out for our Father, we Youth of Harmony!
